      "title": "Counting to fifty",
      "narration": "Is Priya’s bakery a small employer? Maryland defines a small employer as one that employed an average of not more than 50 employees during the preceding calendar year. The count is full-time employees, those averaging 30 or more hours a week, plus full-time equivalents, calculated each month by dividing the hours of part-time employees by 120. Seasonal workers are excluded. Priya has 14 full-time workers and six part-timers at 20 hours a week, about 480 part-time hours a month, which is four full-time equivalents. Eighteen in all: a small employer. A firm with 60 full-time workers is a large group.",
