      "title": "Guaranteed availability",
      "narration": "A carrier that sells small group coverage in Maryland must accept every small employer that applies and meets its uniformly applied participation and contribution requirements, and must enroll every eligible employee the employer offers coverage to. It may not deny, limit or condition coverage because of the health status of the employer’s workers, and discriminating against employees on the basis of health status is an unfair trade practice. The only lawful reasons to turn down a small group are failure to meet participation or contribution rules, location outside the carrier’s service area or the carrier’s lack of capacity, applied to all groups alike.",
