      "title": "Rating the small group",
      "narration": "Small group premiums are set by modified community rating. For plans issued or renewed since 2014, rates may vary only by whether coverage is individual or family, by rating area, by age within a 3 to 1 ratio for adults, and by tobacco use within 1.5 to 1. Nothing else: not health, not claims, not industry, not gender. Rates are fixed for the entire plan year, so Priya’s premium cannot change midyear when an employee gets sick. Carriers must use accepted actuarial methods and apply risk adjustment consistently. Grandfathered small group plans keep an older Maryland rating structure with limited adjustments.",
