      "narration": "Small group coverage is guaranteed renewable at the employer’s option. A carrier may refuse to renew only for nonpayment of premium, fraud or intentional misrepresentation, failure to meet participation or contribution requirements, the employer leaving the carrier’s service area, or the carrier’s withdrawal from the small group market with the required notice, after which it may not reenter for five years. The group’s claims, the illness of an employee or the age of the workforce are never grounds. Renewal premiums may change within the rating rules. This is HIPAA’s renewability guarantee as implemented in Maryland’s small group law.",
